CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ stoi: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ stoll with index: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ stoul base 16: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
libc++ declares std::stoi and its siblings in <string> and defines them in
libc++.so, so the calls had no body and returned nondeterministic values
(cpp17_stoll_char_literal_overload failed on macOS).
